# Reading RDF 1.2 literal and statement forms
#
# This N-Quads sample stores a name, a language tag, an integer, a title with
# a writing direction, and a reified statement with its source. It supplies
# data representations; the N3 example shows rules that inspect such data.

VERSION "1.2"

# The first three statements use the default graph. The remaining statements
# keep the title and claim evidence in a named graph.
<https://example/alice> <https://example/name> "Alice" .
<https://example/alice> <https://example/label> "Bonjour"@FR .
<https://example/alice> <https://example/age> "42"^^<http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#integer> .
<https://example/document> <https://example/title> "HTML و CSS"@ar--rtl <https://example/graph> .
_:claim <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#reifies> <<( <https://example/alice> <https://example/knows> <https://example/bob> )>> <https://example/graph> .
_:claim <https://example/source> <https://example/chat> <https://example/graph> .
